    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119-a2">

                <pb facs="0181" n="105" xml:id="pg105"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Agriculture and Commerce to Minister
                        Reinsch </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your communication, in which you state that under the terms of the
                    Preliminary Agreement of January 30, 1914, entered into between the Chinese
                    Government and the American Red Cross with respect to the drainage of the Huai
                    River and Grand Canal areas, there are two propositions which may be made. You
                    introduce Messrs. W. F. Carey and E. T. Gregory, representatives of the
                    Siems-Carey Company in China.</p>
                <p>I have referred the matter to Mr. Chin, the Director General of the National
                    Conservancy Bureau, for consideration, and now am in receipt of his reply, a
                    copy of which I now enclose for your consideration.</p>
                <p>With compliments,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chou Tzu-Chi</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
